{{/*
Manual visual regression fixture for go-template-mode fontification.

Open this file in Emacs for visual inspection. It intentionally contains
malformed examples and is not intended for template execution: the referenced
data and functions do not need to exist.

Expected behavior:

1. Ordinary output receives no template-specific face.
2. Actions remain visible inside double-quoted HTML attributes.
3. Strings protect delimiter-looking text inside actions.
4. Current action words and predefined functions are highlighted.
5. HTML tag names receive no package-specific face.
*/}}

==================== Ordinary output text ====================

These are ordinary words, not template syntax:
if range with end block break continue printf slice eq len $outside

Ordinary quoted output should also remain ordinary output:
"if printf $quoted {{if .Enabled}}action inside output quotes{{end}}"

==================== Basic actions ====================

{{if .User}}
  Hello, {{$name := .User.Name}}{{$name}}.
  {{printf "%s" $name}}
{{else}}
  No user was supplied.
{{end}}

{{with .Profile}}
  {{print .DisplayName}}
{{end}}

{{range $index, $item := .Items}}
  {{printf "%d: %s" $index $item}}
{{else}}
  No items.
{{end}}

==================== Whitespace trimming ====================

Before{{- print "trimmed on both sides" -}}After

The minus sign below is a negative number, not a left trim marker:
{{-3}}

==================== Template comments ====================

{{/* One-line comment with if, printf, $variable, and "a string". */}}

{{/* A multiline comment.
Everything here should have the comment face, including {{if .Hidden}},
HTML-looking text such as <div>, and "quoted text".
*/}}

{{- /* Trim-marked template comment. */ -}}

These are not valid template comments and should not get a template-comment face:
plain text /* comment-looking text */
{{ /* whitespace makes this an ordinary, invalid action */ }}

==================== Strings inside actions ====================

The delimiter-looking text inside each string is data, not an action end:
{{printf "%s" "double-quoted }} is still string data"}}
{{printf "%s" `raw }} is still string data`}}
{{printf "%c" '}'}}
{{printf "%s" "escaped quote: \"; braces: }}; still data"}}

The real closing delimiter after each string should receive the delimiter face.

==================== HTML attributes ====================

The actions below should override the surrounding HTML string face:
<div class="{{if .Active}}active{{else}}inactive{{end}}" data-id="{{.ID}}">
  Attribute action test
</div>

<input value="{{.Value}}" disabled="{{not .Enabled}}">

This single-quoted attribute is a useful comparison case:
<a data-label='{{printf "%s" .Label}}'>Label</a>

Actions should remain visible in other quoted output contexts too:
<script>const enabled = "{{if .Enabled}}yes{{else}}no{{end}}";</script>

==================== Action words ====================

{{define "named-template"}}
  Named template body.
{{end}}

{{template "named-template" .}}

{{block "body" .}}
  Default block body.
{{end}}

{{range .Items}}
  {{if .Stop}}{{break}}{{end}}
  {{if .Skip}}{{continue}}{{end}}
  {{print .}}
{{end}}

==================== Predefined functions ====================

Standard predefined functions:
{{and .A .B}}
{{html .Markup}}
{{index .Items 0}}
{{js .Script}}
{{len .Items}}
{{not .Disabled}}
{{or .A .B}}
{{print .Value}}
{{printf "%s" .Value}}
{{println .Value}}
{{urlquery .Query}}

{{call .Function .Argument}}
{{slice .Items 0 2}}
{{eq .A .B}}
{{ne .A .B}}
{{lt .A .B}}
{{le .A .B}}
{{gt .A .B}}
{{ge .A .B}}

Pipeline and parenthesized command:
{{printf "%s" (index .Values 0) | html}}

==================== Constants and variables ====================

{{if true}}{{print nil}}{{else}}{{print false}}{{end}}

Root and named variables:
{{$}}
{{$1}}
{{$name_2}}
{{$x.Field}}
{{$π2}}

Names that only contain a keyword or builtin prefix should not partially match:
{{myrange .Value}}
{{printfx .Value}}
{{length .Value}}

Matching is case-sensitive:
{{IF .Value}}
{{Printf .Value}}

==================== Host-owned HTML tag names ====================

These tag names should receive no package-specific face:
<div>paired</div>
<br>
<img src="example.png">

Custom and uppercase tag names are also owned by the host mode:
<user-card data-id="{{.ID}}">Custom element</user-card>
<SECTION>Uppercase element</SECTION>

No misleading tag-name prefix should receive a template face:
<divine>Not a div element</divine>
<bravo>Not a br element</bravo>
<article>Neither this name nor its "a" prefix is template syntax</article>

==================== Actions in surrounding markup ====================

<!-- {{if .Debug}}Debug output{{end}} -->

<style>
  .status::after { content: "{{if .Ready}}ready{{else}}waiting{{end}}"; }
</style>

==================== Unterminated input ====================

This final construct intentionally has no closing comment delimiter and should
remain unfontified through the end of the buffer.

